We've just released MailStripper Pro 1.3.0.  A long time in the pipeline,
this version includes many enhancements, bug fixes and new features that make
it far more flexible than ever before.

Some of the changes since 1.2.4 include:
# New scanning core 2-3 times as fast as the previous one.
# Text-mode config tool completely reorganised to follow the GUI
   tool more closely.
# Plug-in interface with published API - this allows MailStripper's
   capabilities to be expanded virtually without restriction.
# SURBL support - handled via a plug-in.
# Local Blocklist support. If you need to make changes for your local
   setup, and want to take the updates from our server, now you can.
# Recipient Taglist - subject line tagging is no longer an all-or-
   nothing setting.
# Solaris-X86 is added to the list of supported platforms, our builds
   are built under Solaris 9.

SOLARIS/SPARC users: We are looking to upgrade the build server to
Solaris 9 - PLEASE get in touch if this will cause you problems.

The complete ChangeLog can be viewed from the Download page on our website, at
http://mailstripper.eridani.co.uk/

-- 
-- Michael "Soruk" McConnell
Eridani Star System

