Anyone interested in this subject -- of digital photography?

The March 2003 issue of DIGIT, the computer magazine, has a very useful 
208-page book that comes free with this month's publication. It is called 'Fast 
Track to Digital Photography'. Some of the subjects it touches on:

 	* Digital Vs Conventional
 	* Low-light Photography
 	* Give Old Images a Makeover
 	* Adding Special Effects
 	* Photo Imaging and Editing
 	* Sharing Your Photos
 	* Camera phone Phonephotography

Some other useful inputs in this issue, a report on the 'Rainbow' handheld ("it 
looks like a PDA, it weighs as much as and feels like one. But functionally, it 
is more like a labtop computer and a mobile phone shrunk into the body of a 
pocket PC. It has been developed by Indian engineers at iWave Systems 
Technologies, an up-and-coming embedded products firm based in Bangalore... The 
'Rainbow' handheld mobility platform is one of the first devices in the world 
to exploit the power of a new chip.... It is one of the first handhelds to 
exploit the Linus OS..")

Is the last statement true?

Here are some useful software from the world of GNU/Linux, on this month's 
DIGIT's DVD/CD:

* MPlayer 1.0 pres6a
* MPlayer 1.0 pre6a Source Code
* 15 MPlayer skins
* MPlayer manual
* ProZilla 1.3.3
* ProZilla GUI
* GNUsound 0.6.2
* Blender 2.2.5 (there's a tutorial for this in March CHIP!)
* Yafray 0.0.7-2
* Kino
* mythTV
* mythTV Modules
* Skype 1.0 (for Mandrake 10.1 and FC3)

Regards, FN
